<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mixed constitution</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A mixed constitution is a form of government combining elements of monarchy, aristocracy and democracy, so that each checks the others. Ancient writers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristotle">Aristotle</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a> praised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> for such a constitution. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>, power was shared among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suffete">suffetes</a>, the council of elders and the popular assembly.</p></div>
